09:05 < fjahr> #topic ask about testnet5 progress (darosior)
09:06 -!- l0rinc [~l0rinc@user/l0rinc] has joined #bitcoin-core-dev
09:06 < darosior> So my understanding is that progress was blocked on my BIP 54 PR, which is now open. So i'm curious what people working on testnet5 are planning
09:07 -!- PaperSword [~Thunderbi@securemail.qrsnap.io] has quit [Ping timeout: 267 seconds]
09:07 -!- kevkevin [~kevkevin@99-191-131-230.lightspeed.cicril.sbcglobal.net] has quit [Remote host closed the connection]
09:07 < darosior> In particular regarding the genesis block, since that's probably the real "release" of the new testnet
09:07 < fjahr> I have a branch prepared with all the manual stuff that was needed for testnet4, so I think I can open a draft by the end of the week, I was just travelling and busy with publishing CISA stuff which I wanted to get out in time for a conference
09:07 -!- sr_gi [~sr_gi@46.231.244.218] has joined #bitcoin-core-dev
09:08 < darosior> One challenge i see is that if the testnet5 PR is based on top of my BIP 54 PR, it will probably not make it in before feature freeze
09:08 -!- Guest71 [~Guest71@73.43.65.14] has joined #bitcoin-core-dev
09:08 < darosior> fjahr: cool
09:08 -!- sr_gi [~sr_gi@46.231.244.218] has quit [Client Quit]
09:08 < fjahr> Someone volunteered to mine the genesis block already, I guess we will put that in the pull at the last minute when it has been reviewed, when it's out things will probably take a life of their own as was the case with Testnet 4, I think the release isn't really that imporatant in this case
09:09 -!- sr_gi [~sr_gi@109.38.151.27] has joined #bitcoin-core-dev
09:09 < darosior> Ok, so are we fine with starting testnet5 even if the option to use it doesn't make it in a release before something like 8 months?
09:10 < darosior> Anybody else has opinions on this? I pinged Fabian and Pol before the meeting but i wanted to bring it up to the group here too
09:10 < sliv3r__> If we are ok with that, what happens if people start mining on top of the T5 genesis block a chain that is BIP54 invalid?
09:10 < Murch[m]> Sorry, I don't understand the problem
09:10 -!- l0rinc [~l0rinc@user/l0rinc] has quit [Ping timeout: 261 seconds]
09:11 < darosior> sliv3r__: i was assuming you'd base the T5 PR on top of the BIP 54 implementation, since that what you previously told me you'd prefer
09:11 < Murch[m]> Why can't we ship support for testnet5 in v32, even if bip54 support only ships in v33?
09:11 < sliv3r__> would we release it enforcing it from genesis thus Core invalidating the whole chain and making miners start again?
09:11 < fjahr> I guess we can discuss that further in the draft pull before it has the genesis block included. If reviewer turnaround is quick maybe we can still make it, I don't have a strong opinion because with T4 people just started using it before the release
09:12 < darosior> Murch[m]: i think sliv3r__ and fjahr strongly prefer to have bip 54 activated from genesis on testnet5, because that is what the BIP prescribes
09:12 -!- Guest13 [~Guest97@49.207.149.190] has joined #bitcoin-core-dev
09:12 < fjahr> The review should be pretty straight forward because it builds on the Testnet 4 changes and is mostly identical
09:12 < andrewtoth_> so if there's a dependency on the BIP54 PR then there's no chance the testnet5 PR will make it for v32
